<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Järvamaa</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inland county at the heart of Estonia, conquered in the early 13th century and later a key holding of the Livonian Order.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Järvamaa</a>, Jerwia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, occupied the central plateau of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>, bordering most of the other Estonian lands. Its central position made it a crossroads, and it appears often in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia's</a> chronicle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Järvamaa's</a> elders joined the alliances of the Estonian counties against the crusaders and their Latvian allies. Its people farmed the limestone plateau and maintained hillforts as places of refuge. Its leaders accepted baptism after repeated raids around 1220.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Fought over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Järvamaa</a> was assigned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stensby">Treaty of Stensby</a> in 1238. The Order built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paide">Weissenstein</a> (Paide) castle there in 1265, and the region remained Order territory until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jarvamaa.jpg" alt="Järvamaa" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Hannu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tammsaare-P%C3%B5hja_farm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jerwia, Järva</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=jarvamaa" aria-label="Järvamaa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5221 195 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Järvamaa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5541 451h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5541 451h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=jarvamaa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

